---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { supportContact } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach plank.to with ideas, suggestions, problems, accessibility feedback, or privacy questions."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Ideas, suggestions, problems, and accessibility feedback are all welcome. Every message is
      read.
    </p>

    <h2 id="route">Email us</h2>
    {supportContact.isPlaceholder && (
      <p class="note">
        <strong>Not live yet.</strong> The address below has been chosen, but its mailbox is not set
        up yet, so please do not send messages to it.
      </p>
    )}
    <p>
      Contact:
      {supportContact.href ? (
        <a href={supportContact.href}>{supportContact.value}</a>
      ) : (
        <strong>{supportContact.value}</strong>
      )}
    </p>

    <h2 id="in-app">From inside the app</h2>
    <p>
      In the app, open <strong>Settings</strong> and choose "Suggest a feature or improvement" or
      "Report a problem" under <strong>Feedback</strong>. The app writes the email for you and opens
      it in your mail app. Nothing is sent until you press Send there. If no mail app is set up on
      your device, the app shows this address so you can copy it, and you can write from any email
      account.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what">What to include</h2>
    <h3>An idea or suggestion</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>What you would like the app to do, or what could work better.</li>
      <li>When it would help you, for example "on school mornings" or "when plans change".</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>A problem</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>What you were trying to do and what happened instead.</li>
      <li>
        Your device, operating system version, app version, and text size setting, if you are
        comfortable sharing them. When you write from the app, these are added for you, and you can
        turn them off with "Include device details".
      </li>
      <li>For accessibility issues, any assistive technology you use.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Please do not send planner contents or personal details you do not want to share. The app
      never adds your tasks, routines, location, or clothing choices to an email, and the website
      cannot see your planner data.
    </p>

    <p>
      See also <a href="/help/">Help</a>, <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility</a>, and the{' '}
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
